2) Signal and alert table derived from {{SLO_SLI}}: signal, threshold, severity, operational meaning, and immediate action; distinguish what pages from what only notifies.
3) Incident catalog based on {{INCIDENTES_PRIORITARIOS}}, covering at least: high latency, elevated 5xx errors, CPU/memory saturation, database connection exhaustion, queue backlog or downed consumer, and degraded external dependency. Per incident: symptoms, hypotheses ordered by probability, numbered diagnosis with exact command and expected result, numbered mitigation with expected result, verification of resolution, and escalation per {{POLITICA_ESCALAMIENTO}}. Mark irreversible or high-impact actions.
4) Safe operation procedures: rollback, controlled restart, shutdown feature flag, traffic draining, and horizontal scaling, each with preconditions, steps, risks, and how to abort.
