2. Diagnosis: trace the real SQL ({{LOG_SQL_O_TRAZA}}) or the expected SQL per case, quantify the queries (1 + N), identify each N+1 by origin (per-row resolution, lazy during serialization, lazy outside session or context) and each over-fetching (EAGER by default, heavy columns, joins exceeding what the case consumes) against {{OBJETIVO_CARGA}}. Point to the responsible line or mapping.
