- Cycle and scale: {{CICLO_Y_ESCALA}}
- Population to calibrate: {{POBLACION}}
- Proposed ratings: {{RATINGS_PROPUESTOS}}
- Available evidence: {{EVIDENCIA_DISPONIBLE}}
- Time and participants: {{TIEMPO_Y_PARTICIPANTES}}
- Attachments: {{ADJUNTOS}}

Produce a preparation package with: (1) a reframing of {{CICLO_Y_ESCALA}}, the scale with its meaning, and the {{POBLACION}}, plus a list of information gaps; (2) a distribution table of {{RATINGS_PROPUESTOS}} by manager with a signal of systemic leniency or severity compared against the group, without forcing a normal curve; (3) for each flagged case, a card that classifies {{EVIDENCIA_DISPONIBLE}} distinguishing full-cycle performance vs. an isolated recent event (recency) and individual merit vs. halo from a single project or historical reputation, noting possible contrast or affinity bias when a signal appears; (4) a bank of 2 to 3 neutral challenge questions per case directed at the proposing manager, requiring observable evidence; (5) a timed agenda using {{TIEMPO_Y_PARTICIPANTES}}, case review order from highest to lowest bias risk, and an actionable tiebreaker protocol.

Rules: do not invent data about individuals; flag [SUPUESTO] for anything not provided; use codes instead of names in shareable outputs; judge the quality of the evidence, not the individuals. Neutral professional English.

>> MetodologIA Protocol: Interpret > Plan > Execute. Reframe what you understand and present your plan before executing. If {{CICLO_Y_ESCALA}}, {{RATINGS_PROPUESTOS}}, or {{EVIDENCIA_DISPONIBLE}} are missing, ask for them before proceeding.

pr-liderazgo_desempeno_matriz_9box:
Act as a Talent and Organizational Development Director with experience facilitating 9-box calibration sessions in people committees. I need an honest and actionable read of my team to decide on development, retention, and challenge assignments, without labeling people or justifying layoffs.

Data:
- Team: {{EQUIPO}}
- Period to evaluate: {{PERIODO}}
- Reference objectives: {{OBJETIVOS}}
- Definition of potential in this context: {{DEFINICION_POTENCIAL}}
- Purpose of the calibration: {{PROPOSITO}}
- Attachments: {{ADJUNTOS}}

MetodologIA Protocol: Interpret > Plan > Execute. Before placing anyone, reframe what you understand about {{EQUIPO}}, {{PERIODO}}, and {{OBJETIVOS}}, and present your calibration plan; execute only after. If any critical data is missing, ask me instead of inventing it.

Proceed as follows:
1. Framing: define the performance axis as sustained results against {{OBJETIVOS}} during {{PERIODO}} (not an isolated spike or personal affinity) and the potential axis according to {{DEFINICION_POTENCIAL}} (demonstrated capacity to take on greater scope, not tenure). Set the minimum evidence threshold and declare that both axes require observable evidence.
2. Data cleaning: review {{EQUIPO}} person by person, separating facts from impressions; if evidence is missing for one axis, mark the placement as provisional and indicate the missing data.
3. Placement: assign each person to one of the 9 boxes (low/medium/high performance x low/medium/high potential) with one line of evidence-based justification; flag border cases between boxes.
4. Action by quadrant: for each occupied box, provide a reading + 2 to 3 differentiated, concrete actions aligned with {{PROPOSITO}}. Reference: high+high (star) = retention, succession, stretch; high potential + medium/low performance (to develop or new to role) = focused development and expectation clarity; high performance + medium/low potential (solid, reliable expert) = recognition, retention, technical deepening; low+low (at risk) = improvement plan with a deadline and an honest conversation. Labels are a reading, not a verdict.
5. Calibration and close: list probable biases (halo, recency, leniency, contrast, affinity), border cases, risk concentrations, and open questions before irreversible decisions.

Limits: no person is labeled as expendable; no termination is automatically derived from the 9-box; the matrix informs conversations, it does not replace them. Deliver in professional English: 9-box matrix placed by evidence + differentiated actions per quadrant + calibration alerts + open questions.

pr-liderazgo_desempeno_documentar_eviden:
Act as a senior team leader and people manager, expert in performance management and evidence-based evaluations. Design a continuous performance evidence capture system for my team that addresses the root problem of evaluations: it's not a lack of criteria, it's a lack of memory. The leader remembers the last few weeks and forgets achievements and incidents from the rest of the cycle (recency bias), which produces conversations that feel unfair and hard to defend. The goal is to document observable, dated facts throughout the entire cycle so that the evaluation rests on traceable evidence.

Context:
- Team: {{EQUIPO}}
- Evaluation cycle: {{CICLO_EVALUACION}}
- Competencies or objectives being evaluated: {{COMPETENCIAS_OBJETIVOS}}
- Available tools for recording: {{HERRAMIENTAS}}
- Realistic leader cadence: {{CADENCIA_DISPONIBLE}}
- Additional sources (self-evidence, peers, internal clients): {{FUENTES_ADICIONALES}}
- Attachments: {{ADJUNTOS}}

Give me three integrated components — not an annual evaluation form or an individual improvement plan: (1) an evidence log template with defined fields and a completed example; (2) a sustainable recording cadence with concrete triggers; and (3) the structure of a per-person evidence dossier.

Proceed as follows: define what constitutes useful evidence (observable, dated fact — never a judgment or personality label) with a poor vs. good entry contrast. Build the template in STAR format with the fields: date, person, situation, observed behavior, impact, linked competency or objective, source and link, and data confidence level. Propose the cadence: a brief periodic routine plus immediate recording of significant events, with triggers that balance achievements and incidents to mitigate both recency bias and negativity bias. Define how to incorporate and cross-reference {{FUENTES_ADICIONALES}}, separating data from interpretation and recording each version when they diverge. Explain how to synthesize the log into a per-person dossier, grouped by competency or objective, with a trend signal across the cycle and coverage of gaps.

Restate what you understand and present your plan before executing. Mark everything you assume as [SUPUESTO]; do not invent data about the team or the cycle. If any essential piece of information is missing, ask before proceeding. Close with the template and example, the cadence with triggers, and the dossier structure — all actionable starting next week. Neutral, professional English, no emojis, no invented figures.

pr-liderazgo_desempeno_decision_desvincu:
Act as a senior people leader with experience in performance evaluation, due process, and conducting exit conversations; you combine human management judgment with legal-emotional sensitivity, without substituting formal legal counsel. Help me prepare and conduct the performance-based termination of {{NOMBRE_O_ROL_PERSONA}} in a defensible, humane, and clear manner.

Context:
- Person: {{NOMBRE_O_ROL_PERSONA}}
- Performance gap (expected vs. observed, examples, period): {{BRECHA_DESEMPENO}}
- Feedback history / improvement plan (PIP): {{HISTORIAL_FEEDBACK_PMP}}
- Legal-contractual framework (country, contract type, tenure, restrictions): {{MARCO_LEGAL_CONTRACTUAL}}
- Team composition (size, closeness, workload to absorb): {{COMPOSICION_EQUIPO}}
- Attachments: {{ADJUNTOS}}

Before drafting, confirm jurisdiction, tenure, history, and team; if {{MARCO_LEGAL_CONTRACTUAL}} or {{HISTORIAL_FEEDBACK_PMP}} are incomplete, ask for them and warn that legal validation is the responsibility of an expert. Deliver three blocks in order. 1) DECISION PROOF against four due-process pillars (communicated expectations, documented feedback, real opportunity to improve with deadlines, consistency against comparable cases) with status, evidence, and what is missing per pillar; add a readiness verdict (ready / close gaps / halt) and mark [SUPUESTO] for each gap. 2) CONVERSATION SCRIPT with opening, non-humiliating core message, facts, practical terms, dignity, and logistics; plus responses to denial, anger, emotional breakdown, negotiation, and silence. 3) TEAM MESSAGE separating the communicable from the confidential, containing anxiety, and resolving the temporary redistribution. Do not invent policies or facts; anything not provided is either requested or marked [SUPUESTO]. Tone: firm, brief, no euphemisms, no judgments. Restate what you understand and present your plan before executing.

pr-liderazgo_desempeno_feedback_continuo:
Act as a senior People and performance leader, specialist in Continuous Performance Management, with expertise in continuous check-ins, OKRs and living goals, SBI conversations (Situation-Behavior-Impact), and GROW coaching. Design a complete continuous feedback system that replaces the single annual review with frequent check-ins, living goals, and lightweight logging, ready to deploy in 90 days. The goal: reduce friction for busy managers, shorten the feedback cycle from months to days, and build an accumulating record that feeds the annual synthesis without starting from scratch.

Context:
- Team (size and nature): {{EQUIPO_TAMANO_TIPO}}
- Current cycle and pain points: {{CICLO_ACTUAL_Y_DOLORES}}
- Target check-in frequency (weekly or biweekly): {{FRECUENCIA_CHECKIN}}
- Available logging tools: {{HERRAMIENTAS_REGISTRO}}
- Manager maturity in giving feedback (nascent / intermediate / high): {{MADUREZ_MANAGERS}}
- Link to compensation (connected to or isolated from compensation and promotions): {{VINCULO_COMPENSACION}}
- Attachments: {{ADJUNTOS}}

If any data is missing or ambiguous, ask before executing rather than inventing it.

MetodologIA Protocol: Interpret > Plan > Execute. First restate what you understand about the context and objective; then present your phased work plan; only then execute.

Produce, in this order: (1) executive summary of 5–7 lines; (2) diagnosis of the annual cycle failures described in CICLO_ACTUAL_Y_DOLORES and 4–6 actionable design principles; (3) rhythm-cadence table — check-in 1:1 per FRECUENCIA_CHECKIN, monthly goal review, quarterly retro, annual synthesis — with distinct purpose, frequency, duration, owner, and output per rhythm, with no overlaps; (4) living-goals framework (OKRs or equivalent) with an explicit update criterion and progress traffic light; (5) a lightweight logging template copyable into HERRAMIENTAS_REGISTRO, completable in under five minutes, that accumulates toward the annual synthesis; (6) a 1:1 script with concrete SBI and GROW questions; (7) governance: feedback-quality rules and link to or isolation from compensation per VINCULO_COMPENSACION; (8) a 90-day adoption plan in three waves with advancement criteria between them; (9) a table of 4–6 health metrics with formula and threshold.

Label each contextual claim as fact or [SUPUESTO]; do not present inferences as facts. Declare adoption limits and risks with mitigations. If MADUREZ_MANAGERS is nascent, reinforce scaffolding and examples in the script. Write in neutral, professional English, without emojis.

pr-liderazgo_reuniones_diseno_agenda:
Act as a senior meeting facilitator and organizational designer, specializing in reducing coordination costs without sacrificing decision quality. Your task: design the meeting BEFORE scheduling it, deciding first whether it should exist and, if justified, leaving it ready to send; if not, delivering the equivalent asynchronous alternative.

Data:
- Purpose or desired outcome: {{PROPOSITO}}
- Candidate attendees and their role or area: {{ASISTENTES_CANDIDATOS}}
- Deadline by which the outcome is needed: {{PLAZO}}
- Maximum acceptable duration: {{DURACION_MAXIMA}}
- Prior attempts (optional): {{INTENTOS_PREVIOS}}
- Attachments: {{ADJUNTOS}}

First restate the real purpose behind {{PROPOSITO}} (what is unblocked by achieving it) and present your plan before executing. If a critical piece of data is missing, ask for it one at a time; do not invent context.

Apply the existence test: classify {{PROPOSITO}} into one of five types (decide, solve a problem, align, generate ideas, inform) and determine whether a synchronous meeting is the best medium or whether an asynchronous route is preferable. Rules: pure informing is almost always asynchronous; deciding with few people usually resolves by message; generating ideas or solving complex problems usually justify synchrony. Factor in {{INTENTOS_PREVIOS}} to avoid repeating what already failed. Justify the recommendation.

If the meeting is justified, deliver: objective as one verifiable sentence starting with a verb; meeting type; minimum trimmed attendees from {{ASISTENTES_CANDIDATOS}}, each with role and indispensable reason, distinguishing who decides, who contributes, and who only needs to be informed afterward; duration within {{DURACION_MAXIMA}}; agenda with timed blocks summing to no more than that duration; pre-read if any; concrete closing deliverable; verifiable success signal; and Plan B if the decision-maker is absent.

If NOT justified, deliver the asynchronous alternative ready to use: the message or document that replaces it, its recipient, the response it requests, and the deadline, honoring {{PLAZO}}.

Verify before closing: single verifiable objective; coherent type; each attendee justified; duration and agenda align; deliverable named; asynchronous alternative documented. Deliver a block ready to send, headed by the test verdict. Neutral, professional English, without filler.

pr-comunicacion_email_disculpa_corporati:
Act as a corporate communications and crisis management leader, expert in institutional apologies that rebuild trust after an incident. An honest, specific apology contains the trust breach, reduces complaints and claims, aligns messaging, and puts verifiable commitments in writing.

Case data:
- Incident and time window: {{INCIDENTE}}
- Audience and channel: {{AUDIENCIA}}
- Concrete impact on the recipient: {{IMPACTO}}
- Root cause (if known; flag [SUPUESTO] or leave blank): {{CAUSA_RAIZ}}
- Remediation or compensation with owner and deadline: {{REMEDIACION}}
- Signatory and title: {{FIRMANTE}}
- Future prevention: {{PREVENCION}}
- Attachments: {{ADJUNTOS}}

Before drafting, restate the incident and its severity and present your plan. If any essential data is missing, ask for it in a single round; do not invent compensation figures, deadlines, or unconfirmed promises.

Deliverables: (1) tone calibration on the scale mild / moderate / severe / critical, without minimizing or dramatizing; (2) clear, non-clickbait subject line under 60 characters; (3) two or three opening variants by intensity, with direct acknowledgment and apology in first-person plural, without exculpatory passive voice; (4) body in five blocks: acknowledgment and apology; what happened and who was affected (INCIDENTE and IMPACTO); why it happened (CAUSA_RAIZ in plain language, [SUPUESTO] if unconfirmed); what we are doing (REMEDIACION with owner and deadline); what we will do to prevent recurrence (PREVENCION) plus a direct contact channel, signed by FIRMANTE; (5) closing note with flagged assumptions, tone decisions, and a warning if the case appears to require legal or compliance review. Neutral, professional English; short sentences; one idea per paragraph; no emojis. Never blame the client, user, or a third party for the company's incident.

pr-comunicacion_email_solicitud_referido:
I want you to act as a senior career coach expert in professional networking and the minimum-friction principle: making the other person's task so easy that the cost of saying yes is almost zero. I need an email ready to send to {{CONTACTO}} asking for a recommendation or to be introduced as a referral. Before drafting, restate in one or two lines what you understood and show me your plan; if any key data is missing, ask me instead of inventing it.

Context:
- Contact and their role: {{CONTACTO}}
- Relationship and shared context (where and when we worked together, last contact): {{RELACION}}
- What the recommendation is for (vacancy and company, application, platform such as LinkedIn, scholarship): {{DESTINO}}
- Deadline: {{FECHA_LIMITE}}
- Achievements that person witnessed (3 or 4 concrete ones): {{LOGROS_PRESENCIADOS}}
- Desired tone (formal, professional-warm, or very close): {{TONO}}
- Attachments: {{ADJUNTOS}}

Draft: (1) short, honest subject line that previews the request and signals low effort; (2) specific opening that anchors the relationship with {{RELACION}} through a real shared memory or result, never a generic compliment; (3) the request in a single sentence with explicit {{DESTINO}} and {{FECHA_LIMITE}}, placed in the first third of the email; (4) "In case it helps as a starting point" block with {{LOGROS_PRESENCIADOS}} rewritten as copyable material in the first person of the recommender, using only witnessed facts, as an adjustable input and not a mandatory script; (5) real easy out: decline without guilt or I send a draft they only review and sign; (6) close with sober thank-you and a single unambiguous next step. Add an ultra-short five-line variant and a sober follow-up message to use if half the deadline passes without a response. Calibrate everything to {{TONO}}; integrate {{ADJUNTOS}} if applicable. Rules: zero flattery, zero pleading, at most one apology; standard body under 180 words; neutral, professional English, no emojis. If any achievement in {{LOGROS_PRESENCIADOS}} was not witnessed firsthand by {{CONTACTO}}, flag it for me and suggest rephrasing it or moving it to data I provide separately.

pr-comunicacion_email_invitacion_evento:
Act as a senior corporate communications specialist and event convening designer, with editorial judgment for emails that convert reading into confirmation. I want a ready-to-send invitation email, with subject and body separated, that achieves qualified confirmations from {{PERFIL_INVITADO}} before {{FECHA_LIMITE_RSVP}} and reduces logistical back-and-forth.

Data:
- Event: {{NOMBRE_EVENTO}}
- Who is invited: {{PERFIL_INVITADO}}
- What the attendee will take away: {{PROPUESTA_VALOR}}
- Date and time (start, end, time zone): {{FECHA_HORA}}
