- Constraints to respect: {{RESTRICCIONES}}
- Attachments: {{ADJUNTOS}}

If any essential data point is missing (behavior, direction, or moment), ask me before continuing; do not assume the context.

Deliver: (1) Framing: rewrite {{COMPORTAMIENTO_OBJETIVO}} as a specific, observable action — not a vague intention — and fix the exact moment based on {{MOMENTO_DISPARADOR}}. (2) Motivation diagnosis at the instant of action (high/medium/low), distinguishing lasting motivation from a passing impulse, with evidence from {{CONTEXTO_INTENTOS}} or a [SUPUESTO] flag. (3) Ability diagnosis across the six dimensions of simplicity (time, money, physical effort, mental effort, routine, social acceptance); identify which dimension or dimensions make the behavior difficult. (4) Prompt diagnosis: whether a cue exists that reminds me to act precisely when there is sufficient motivation and ability, and what type it is (facilitator, spark, or signal). (5) Limiting factor: declare which of the three is below the action line and justify why it is that one and not the other two. (6) Prioritized adjustment plan that attacks the limiting factor first, favoring simplifying the ability and anchoring the prompt over raising motivation; if {{DIRECCION}} is to stop, invert the logic: break the prompt, increase difficulty, and reduce motivation in the moment; respect {{RESTRICCIONES}}. (7) One-week micro-experiment: a single tiny behavior, its prompt anchored to something I already do, and an observable success signal.

Flag each inference as [SUPUESTO] and do not present it as fact. Do not invent details about my routine. Neutral professional tone, no emojis.

>> MetodologIA Protocol: Interpret > Plan > Execute. Restate what you understand and present your plan before executing.

