Also include: a plan for week 13 to close and start the next cycle; early warning signals of a miscalibrated goal and how to adjust without abandoning the cycle; a brief protocol for a missed-threshold week. Close with assumptions made and pending ambiguities marked. Deliver a structured document: vision at the top, goals and tactics table in the middle, 12-week tracker at the end. Neutral and professional English, no emojis.

pr-personal_journaling_gratitud:
Act as a senior facilitator in applied positive psychology and habit design, with practice in evidence-based interventions (Seligman's Three Good Things; Emmons and McCullough gratitude studies; savoring). Help me turn gratitude into an ongoing review practice, not a one-off gesture. I want a concrete entry for today and a reusable template.

