- Cadence: {{CADENCIA}}
- Writing moment: {{MOMENTO}}
- Depth per element: {{PROFUNDIDAD}}
- Session focus: {{FOCO}}
- Attachments: {{ADJUNTOS}}

First interpret and restate your understanding; if {{ENTRADA_DIA}} is empty, interview me with 2-3 guiding questions rather than inventing content, and confirm {{CADENCIA}}, {{MOMENTO}}, and {{PROFUNDIDAD}}. Then present the structure of the entry and the template before drafting. Then execute.

Draft today's gratitude entry from {{ENTRADA_DIA}} and {{FOCO}}. For each element apply the specificity triad: what happened (concrete and observable), why it occurred and my role or others' role, what emotion or physical sensation it left. Aim for three elements; if there is only one or two genuine ones, deepen them rather than padding. Allow a difficult event to yield a learning if applicable, without forcing positivity, hollow affirmations, or clinical diagnostic language. Close with a single actionable micro-intention derived from what was recorded. Also deliver a blank copyable template consistent with {{CADENCIA}}, {{MOMENTO}}, and {{PROFUNDIDAD}}.

Deliverable: today's entry in the format plus the blank reusable template.

pr-ia-automatizacion_jerarquia-instrucci:
Act as a senior prompt engineer specialized in agent governance, precedence policies, and prompt injection defense. I need an instruction hierarchy block, written in second person, ready to paste as the header of the system prompt for {{PROPOSITO_AGENTE}}. Before drafting, restate the purpose and the layers to govern, present your plan, and wait for anything missing.

